# Force LF on checkout for source + scripts, regardless of core.autocrlf.
# Two concrete failures this prevents on a Windows checkout:
#  - vite-node mis-parses a CRLF .mjs that carries a SHEBANG: its shebang strip
#    leaves a stray CR behind → "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token", so
#    `npm test` fails on a fresh clone. (Isolated by experiment: the shebang is
#    the trigger; non-ASCII/emoji in a CRLF module parse fine. An earlier
#    revision of this comment blamed the emoji — it was wrong.) The belt is this
#    eol=lf; the braces is keeping shebangs out of imported modules — see the
#    hooks/session-brief.mjs ↔ src/session-brief-core.mjs split.
#  - the bash git hooks under aiteam/githooks/ fail outright if CRLF reaches
#    their shebang/commands.
# Personas e seus bindings gerados: o sync compara conteúdo byte a byte para
# detectar drift, então o checkout não pode reescrever as quebras de linha —
# senão Windows e Linux discordam sobre um arquivo idêntico.
aiteam/agents/*.md text eol=lf
.claude/agents/*.md text eol=lf
# SPEC.md: o frontmatter decide o break-glass allow_tier3, o budget_usd e o
# infra_kb. Os leitores do framework já toleram CRLF (rb-ai-team#36); o LF é a
# defesa em profundidade, para leitor nenhum do SPEC depender disso.
SPEC.md text eol=lf
# Mapa de tiers: o template que viaja com o vendor e a cópia da raiz do upstream
# são iguais byte a byte (aiteam/src/tier-rules-template.test.ts), e o install
# semeia o template como está — LF na cópia de trabalho para as duas.
aiteam/templates/tier-rules.json text eol=lf
.claude/tier-rules.json text eol=lf

*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf
*.ts  text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
aiteam/githooks/* text eol=lf
